; THE HEXA (GAMEPLAY-DESIGN Iteration 17 / E.q1) — six rotors on a ring, and
; EXPERIMENTAL. The user asked for it as *"a very interesting experiment... a low
; priority for now, but a very interesting direction to have fun with, and which
; also pushes us to the simulation direction"*.
;
; EVERY FLIGHT NUMBER HERE IS THE KESTREL'S, DELIBERATELY AND WITHOUT EXCEPTION.
; This is the same 0.28 m, 0.65 kg, TWR-4.5 airframe with two more rotors, so
; that the ONLY variable between it and the datum is the layout. A hexa that also
; changed mass, TWR or rates would be an interesting aircraft and a useless
; experiment, because nothing it did could be attributed to having six rotors.
;
; **TWO NUMBERS ARE KNOWN TO BE WRONG FOR IT AND ARE LEFT ALONE ON PURPOSE**,
; because they are flight feel and flight feel is the human's:
;
;   `yaw_authority` 1.5 is a quad number. Yaw torque is the summed signed rotor
;   output, so a 3+3 split sums to +/-6 at full differential where the quad sums
;   to +/-4 — this frame has roughly 1.5x the yaw authority of the Kestrel from
;   the identical constant. It needs re-tuning by hand, and the direction is
;   down.
;
;   The rate gains are a quad's. The mixer commands each rotor in proportion to
;   its real moment arm, and a generated ring sits at sqrt(2) arm-lengths where
;   the quad-X's corners sit at 1 along each axis, so the same `rate_p` produces
;   a larger commanded spread on this frame. Expect it to feel twitchier than the
;   Kestrel before anyone touches it.
;
; The user's own description was *"a HEXA (6, heavy and slow)"*. It is NOT heavy
; and slow yet — making it so means changing mass and TWR, which is exactly the
; kind of change that wants hands on sticks first.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="FlightConfig" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://resources/flight_config.gd" id="1_cfg"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_cfg")
frame_id = &"hexa"
mass = 0.65
arm_length = 0.12
body_m = 0.28
rotor_layout = &"hex_x"
thrust_to_weight_ratio = 4.5
motor_lag_tau = 0.05
motor_idle = 0.05
yaw_authority = 1.5
reverse_thrust_scale = 0.8
max_rate_deg = Vector3(580, 580, 550)
expo = Vector3(0.3, 0.3, 0.3)
gyro_lpf_hz = 90.0
dterm_lpf_hz = 70.0
rc_smoothing_hz = 0.0
rate_p = Vector3(0.007, 0.007, 0.007)
rate_i = Vector3(0.002, 0.002, 0.002)
rate_d = Vector3(3e-05, 3e-05, 3e-05)
rate_ff = Vector3(0.0008, 0.0008, 0.0008)
ff_lpf_hz = 20.0
integral_limit = 0.2
crash_iterm_decay = 1.0
iterm_error_gate_deg = 300.0
iterm_relax_hz = 15.0
iterm_relax_threshold_deg = 40.0
input_profile = 0
stick_deadzone = 0.08
throttle_curve = 2
max_angle_deg = 56.0
angle_p = 6.0
drag_coefficient = 0.03
angular_damping = 0.013
fpv_offset = Vector3(0, 0.03, -0.08)
fpv_uptilt_deg = 48.0
fpv_fov_deg = 94.0
chase_distance = 3.5
chase_height = 1.2
chase_smoothing = 8.0
pause_time_scale = 0.03
autopilot_tilt_deg_per_ms = 4.0
autopilot_climb_gain = 0.08
arm_throttle_threshold = 0.05
